From 4b37106d055a22101b102df7454bc73c659517ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:42:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] model: offload the input embeddings to the GPU on a single
 device

The input layer (token_embd + per_layer_token_embd) was always left on the CPU
("there is very little benefit to offloading the input layer").  With a single
GPU that meant the token-embedding GET_ROWS was dispatched to the CPU backend,
and on an APU (gfx1151) the CPU backend's OpenMP thread pool spun every core on
every step.  The MTP draft is the visible case: its mtp_tok_embd gather runs
every speculative step, and the hybrid-idx draft graph also puts the
recurrent-state zeroing ops in the same CPU split, so the pool never sleeps
(~11 cores at 100%, ~1060% CPU).

Place the input layer on the output layer's device when the model has a single
GPU, so the GET_ROWS runs on the GPU; multi-GPU setups keep the stock CPU
placement (a host-buffer/device policy per split is a follow-up).

Measured (gfx1151, qwen4exp IQ4_NL + MTP sidecar, -c 16384):
  sparse MTP decode 1068-1090% CPU / 17 busy threads -> 155% / 2 (the ROCm
  runtime's own wait threads), matching the reference fork.
Byte-identical at every gate: 8K 3553e76d3a9e, 40K 8285d12d40ca, 128K
MTP == plain 770e770ae7d6; width probe PASS; imatrix NanBeige BF16 clean and
byte-identical to HC16=0; FLASH_ATTN_QSA/GATED_DELTA_NET green.
---
 src/llama-model.cpp | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-model.cpp b/src/llama-model.cpp
index 9d3bce7a7..8e77afc75 100644
--- a/src/llama-model.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-model.cpp
@@ -1532,9 +1532,16 @@ bool llama_model_base::load_tensors(llama_model_loader & ml) {
         return {dev, &pimpl->gpu_buft_list.at(dev)};
     };
 
-    // assign the input layer
-    // there is very little benefit to offloading the input layer, so always keep it on the CPU
-    pimpl->dev_input = { cpu_dev, &pimpl->cpu_buft_list };
+    // assign the input layer.  With a single GPU the token-embedding weights (token_embd /
+    // per_layer_token_embd) are placed on the output layer's device, so their GET_ROWS runs on the
+    // GPU.  On an APU that avoids dispatching the CPU backend - and spinning its OpenMP thread
+    // pool - on every step (notably the MTP draft's mtp_tok_embd gather).  Multi-GPU setups keep
+    // the stock CPU placement for now.
+    if (n_devices() == 1) {
+        pimpl->dev_input = get_layer_buft_list(n_layer_all);
+    } else {
+        pimpl->dev_input = { cpu_dev, &pimpl->cpu_buft_list };
+    }
 
     // assign the repeating layers to the devices according to the splits
     pimpl->dev_layer.resize(n_layer_all);
